{"study_accession":"PRJNA1344834","secondary_study_accession":"SRP636628","title":"Homo sapiens Raw sequence reads","description":"Mammalian genomes host a diverse array of RNA that includes protein-coding and noncoding transcripts. However, the functional roles of most long noncoding RNAs (lncRNAs) remain elusive. Using RNA-targeting CRISPR-Cas13 screens, we probed how loss of ~5,500 lncRNAs impacts cell fitness across five human cell lines and identified 788 lncRNAs with context-specific or broad essentiality. We confirm their essentiality with individual perturbations and find that the majority of essential lncRNAs operate independently of their nearest protein-coding genes. Using transcriptome profiling in single cells, we discover that loss of essential lncRNAs impair cell cycle progression and drive apoptosis. Many essential lncRNAs demonstrate dynamic expression across tissues during development. Using ~9,000 primary tumors, we pinpoint those lncRNAs whose expression in tumors correlates with survival, yielding new biomarkers and potential therapeutic targets. This transcriptome-wide survey of functional lncRNAs advances our understanding of noncoding transcripts and demonstrates the potential of transcriptome-scale noncoding screens with Cas13.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":11,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN46391779","study_accession":"PRJNA1344834","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","sex":"male","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-01-25","attributes":[["isolate","Replicate 1"],["age","Day00"],["biomaterial_provider","Neville Sanjana"],["collection_date","2021-10-18"],["geo_loc_name","USA: New York"],["sex","male"],["tissue","bone marrow"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR32105813","experiment_accession":"SRX27451354","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"other","instrument_model